V13 resolved the identity crisis. V14 resolves the execution gap. Memory without action is a filing cabinet. V14 names the coordination layer explicitly, fixes the pricing model, sharpens the moat, corrects an overreaching GTM claim, and states the accuracy fallback plainly.
 
| **What changed** | **Why** |
| --- | --- |
| Coordination layer named | Memory alone is passive intelligence. Layer 3 (coordination) is where operational dependency forms. Tasks, owners, reminders, workflow triggers. This is the missing middle between memory and intelligence. |
| Pricing model rebuilt | Flat seat pricing does not match a value-that-compounds product. Two tiers: Founder at €49, Team at €89/seat. First 100 customers grandfathered at €49 flat for 12 months. No overage charges. No AI billing anxiety. |
| Moat articulated precisely | Continuity is not specific enough. The moat is four distinct compounding assets: longitudinal relationship graph, behavioural GTM intelligence, embedded coordination workflows, trust history. |
| GTM claim corrected | V1 claim: Outround prepares every conversation and remembers everything after. Phase 3 claim: Outround also finds and books conversations. These are not the same thing. V14 does not conflate them. |
